   "text": "I read the drawing as a PROTAC-type molecule. A pyridazine warhead is joined through a pyrazole, a phenoxy-ethoxy linker and an isoxazole to a VHL-type hydroxyproline ligand.\n\n**Left side**\n- The pyridazine ring carries an NH2, a 2-hydroxyphenyl group, and the pyrazole at C4.\n- The pyrazole is attached through its C4, and its N1 carries a CH(CH3) group bonded to a para-substituted phenyl ring.\n\n**Linker**\n- The phenyl ring has an O\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013O chain that ends on C3 of an isoxazole.\n\n**Isoxazole to VHL ligand**\n- C5 of the isoxazole bears a CH with an isopropyl group (hashed bond) and a C(=O) bonded to the pyrrolidine nitrogen.\n- Working through the CIP priorities (C(=O) > isoxazole C5 > isopropyl, H toward the viewer), this centre comes out as S.\n- The pyrrolidine has a 4-OH (hashed) and a 2-carboxamide (wedged). I wrote these as the standard (2S,4R) VHL hydroxyproline.\n- The amide nitrogen is attached to an (S)-1-arylethyl group. The aryl is a phenyl bearing a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n- I assigned the pyrrolidine and methylbenzyl stereocentres by matching the drawing to the standard VHL ligand rather than deriving each one independently. I then checked the SMILES atom ordering against that standard.\n\nThe CH(CH3) carbon between the pyrazole and the phenyl ring is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: Nc1nnc(-c2ccccc2O)cc1-c1cnn(C(C)c2ccc(OCCOc3cc([C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N4C[C@H](O)C[C@H]4C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c4ccc(-c5scnc5C)cc4)on3)cc2)c1"
